  "policy": {
    "bounds": "For fulfilled 206 intervals, each endpoint must lie in a parsed requested interval after resolving a known total. Smaller subsets, reordered parts and coalescing across requested intervals are permitted.",
    "suffix": "Known totals resolve suffixes to their last N bytes, clipping longer suffixes to the entire representation. Unknown totals permit only a maximum returned-size check. A zero-length suffix cannot produce a 206.",
    "multipart": "Collect at most 16 parsed intervals. Any known total constrains all parts, including those with an unknown total; apply request-bound checks before MCP returns the complete body.",
    "arithmetic": "Request positions and lengths retain the local signed 63-bit ceiling. Arithmetic uses unsigned Go values or Python integers and does not compute a signed last+1.",
    "context": "A missing request context during the first wire parse is distinct from a known request without Range. Production response validation supplies the original request context.",
    "compatibility": "200 may ignore Range and 416 remains accepted when otherwise valid. Accepted body bytes are preserved. No partial representation reconstruction is performed.",
    "coalescing_limit": "No fixed gap threshold is inferred because the server hypothetical multipart overhead is unavailable. Endpoint containment is a local bounds contract, not proof of every server range-selection requirement."
  },
